From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Open Video Tools contributors <noreply@ovt.dev>
Date: 2026-11-07
Subject: [PATCH] Add a read-only internals API (de265_internals.h)

Adds the CMake option DE265_INTERNALS (default OFF). With it ON, libde265 builds and installs
libde265/de265_internals.h and libde265/de265_internals.cc: C functions that read the
per-picture metadata the decoder already keeps (CTB slice and SAO info, CB size, partition
and prediction mode, PB motion, intra modes, TU split flags, deblocking edge flags, slice
headers) of a picture returned by de265_get_next_picture(). Coordinates are always units of
the layout the matching *_layout() function returns. Consumers: analysis tools such as Open
Video Tools, sherlock265 and YUView.

libde265 keeps one boundary strength per 4x4 block and the horizontal-edge pass overwrites
the vertical-edge value, so the patch adds de265_image::deblk_bS_v and one store in
derive_boundaryStrength() for vertical edges. That is the only change to decoding code, and
like the friend declaration that lets the accessors read the metadata arrays it is compiled
only when DE265_INTERNALS is defined. With DE265_INTERNALS=OFF the library is identical to
upstream (same symbols, same object code).

Every modified upstream file carries a dated modification notice (GPL-3.0 section 5(a),
through LGPL-3.0); the two new files are LGPL-3.0-or-later like libde265.

Upstream-Status: Pending [to be submitted to strukturag/libde265 by WI-2.167]
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The Open Video Tools contributors
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later
Rationale: libde265's public API exposes decoded pictures only; per-block coding data (CB tree,
  motion, intra modes, transform tree, deblocking bS, SAO) lives in private de265_image members
  with no accessor in de265.h (chapter 07 section 7.6.2).
